From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 09:45:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SEARCH-NEAREST-1: deterministic nearest-match repair for an
 invented SEARCH (qnfo-code-orchestrator 0.19.0-search-nearest-1)

Root cause: applyEdits needs a verbatim unique SEARCH and only repaired whitespace,
indentation and (0.18.29) a SEARCH that lies outside the window. A rung that rewrites
a real block from memory with one line reworded still failed the attempt: 90 "SEARCH
text occurs 0 times in the shown content" failures in 7 days to 2026-10-19, 41 in the
last 24 h, mostly gpt-oss-120b.

Measurement (cloud_ops_events code-task.fail + code_tasks.ctx.lastReply, D1 SELECT
only): the messages that count shared lines show real blocks with one line reworded
(4 of 5, 5 of 6, 10 of 11 lines equal) but most misses are another shape: 53 of 75 share
no line with the file, 12 of the 13 stored replies are 1-2 line SEARCH blocks, and
ct_994jv3f6x057tm is a 10-line SEARCH with 5 invented lines (replayed on main: refused,
as intended). The exact-line share has a gap between 0.67 (8/12, 4/6 x3) and 0.80 (4/5,
5/6, 10/11), so the bar is: SEARCH of 3 to 60 lines and 80+ normalised chars, at least
75% of its non-blank lines equal to one window of the same line count, mean line
similarity 0.92 or more (edit-distance ratio), no rival window (another window clearing
the bar, or any within 0.03 of the best). Expected yield is small (about 3 of 90 events
had the shape); the other shapes stay refused with the closest lines named.

Change: applyEdits takes opts.nearest, set only by the propose step after the exact,
indentation, fuzzy and 0.18.29 relocate paths, never for a multi-file task or a file over
the large-file window. nearestReplace aligns SEARCH and REPLACE line by line (longest
common subsequence): every SEARCH line the REPLACE leaves identical is carried through as
the file's own window line at the same offset, so a reworded line the model did not mean
to change (also one between two changed lines) keeps its file text, and only the lines the
REPLACE adds or alters are the model's, re-indented. The parked edits become the file's
own text so verify, commit and the publisher's rebuild apply them exactly, and the repair
is applied only when that rewrite yields the same text. Each repair is the audit event
code-task.edit-nearest with the score, the offsets and the sha-256 of the model's SEARCH
and of the file text. Migration 2026-10-19-search-nearest.sql adds the failure_modes row
code-task-search-invented and the fm-code-task-search-invented detector (regression
guard at 39 in 24 h, counted from 2026-10-19T12:00Z); no hold, filter or cap is added.

Tests: qnfo-code-orchestrator/search-nearest.test.mjs, 23 checks on the real applyEdits
through the task loop. Against origin/main's worker.js: 11 passed, 7 failed (the near
SEARCH spends an attempt and no edit-nearest event exists). Against the first version of
this commit (common top and bottom lines only): the new interior case (change on lines 2
and 4 around a reworded line 3) fails 3 checks, because the model's `Number(row.rank)`
replaced the file's `Number(row.rank || 0)`. With the change: 23 passed. Ambiguous, weak,
2-line and large-file SEARCH are refused as before; exact, indent, fuzzy and relocate
paths never reach the new one. Full orchestrator and scripts suite set: 41 passed, 0 failed.

Refs QNFO/qnfo-workers#2111 (agent_issues 2111, model-edit-format-reliability).

