at timed out (meta.model), so timeouts are graded per model. */ /* 0.18.23 LEASE-FENCE-1 (2026-10-19, pillar autonomy): every save inside a step is fenced on the lease the lane claimed (status queued, lease_until unchanged), and the lease is 5 minutes (was 90 s, under the 106 s and 175 s average calls of two ladder rungs), so a lane whose lease lapsed during a slow model call can no longer overwrite the task another lane already moved on; a fenced save that matches no row ends the stale step with event code-task.lease-lost and writes nothing (ct_zogt4y5sdzauqw: ready_to_publish at 06:26:44Z, then step verify and no ctx.patch from the stale lane, publish_failed at 06:27:31Z; 6 such rows in 48 h). */ /* 0.18.22 MERGE-SCOPE-AT-READ-1 (2026-10-19, agent_issues 99951/2983/3000): mergeScopeWhy normalizes an owner-qualified repo slug and also runs at the read step, so a task written straight into code_tasks on a path the merge runner never merges ends needs_human before any model call. */ /* 0.18.16 MODEL-ATTRIBUTION-1 (2026-10-18): a task that fails at
